    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a derived, read-only field on the owner that carries the Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `customerCode`. The codebase already used a consistent pattern for such derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId`, etc.), so I followed it:\n\n1. **`util/CheckDigits.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper with a `luhn(String)` method that computes the Luhn check digit over the decimal digits in a string, ignoring non-digit characters (the `-` separators in `customerCode`). Its algorithm mirrors the test's reference `luhn` exactly (right-to-left, rightmost digit doubled, `(10 - sum%10) % 10`).\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` that calls `CheckDigits.luhn(owner.getCustomerCode())`, so every serialized owner exposes the check digit.\n\nNo storage was needed since `checkDigit` is fully derived from `customerCode` at serialization time, matching how the other computed owner fields work. The new `Cp31Tests` (which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit) passes, along with all existing tests.",
